{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789751941,"nonce":"i1hnQJCT5A1VJTOoS3GeKCy2FIk=","message":"Implementation (uncommitted at this point): the interpreter holds aggregates as Cranelift does (multi-field struct, array, union by address; a struct of one scalar as that scalar; layout with natural alignment via hir_interp::struct_layout), Load of an aggregate copies into frame scratch, Store copies bytes, ExtractValue/InsertValue read and write in place at the layout offsets, GEP walks pointer/array/struct/byte the way the Cranelift emitter does, undef and constant aggregates get zeroed or filled frame storage, Alloca and copies are released when the frame returns, a destination-returning callee gets storage from the caller. Phi copies are parallel. Free frees through the pool.\n\nBridge: CraneliftBackend::interp_thunk(NativeSig) compiles one fn(target, words, out) per call shape (destination passed first when the callee returns through one, Fast convention honoured); the interpreter calls promoted functions, refused functions (generators, effects), externs (with DynamicBox auto-boxing per the registered ZRTL signature, boxes freed after the call), indirect calls and function addresses (cell content, else the load-time code) through it. Without a thunk source (tests, wasm) the fixed JitDispatch matrix stays.\n\nTiering: beads start without code; the tier-0 (Cranelift baseline) policy is TieredConfig::baseline_threshold (20) calls; an interpreted loop header with a representable layout counts visits and at 256 asks for promotion: the requester compiles the baseline first when the bead has none (off the caller's stack), then force_promote as a tier-0 frame would; the header then polls the same helper slot the Cranelift probes read and transfers through an OsrFrame. The register file of every interpreted frame is a collector root range for the frame's life.\n\nNested loops: an inner header used to be rejected (RegionHasExternalEntry) because the outer header lies in its region and is entered from before the loop. The layout now plans a Repair per live-in the region redefines (a phi at the resume header merging the frame value with the region's definition; reads in header-dominated blocks renamed), and osr::resumable applies it to the function the helper is compiled from; both native helper emitters seed the repaired phis from the frame. Rejection remains only when a read is reached by neither definition alone.\n\nConformance 115/116 on the interpreter tier (int/big_values as before). nbody before the repair: 82 s, main() interpreted with 10 M calls into native advance at ~8 us each through the interpreter's call path.","files":null}]}